From 39a08dd670654603dfa981fcf68ccd19ecf9b2cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 13:26:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] virtio_fs: thirty-two request slots, and their contiguity
 proven

Eight slots meant eight FUSE requests in flight at most -- a Tracker
copy of a folder is a create, data, attributes and times for every file
at once, and each of those is several requests, so a burst of them
queued behind one another. Thirty-two cost 4.25 MiB of contiguous
memory, which the machine has.

The slot area's physical layout was derived from the first page's
address alone; B_CONTIGUOUS promises one physical run, and asking
get_memory_map() for the whole area in one entry now proves it before
any request is ever built from those addresses (a second run would
return B_BUFFER_OVERFLOW instead of silent DMA corruption).

Prose-Patch: 0082-virtio-fs-thirty-two-request-slots-and-their-contiguity-prov.patch d632e611483d255b31147c823e3bbf2c4a516edc08d5e0e1d518c93f40b208ca
---
 .../drivers/disk/virtual/virtio_fs/virtio_fs.cpp     | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/disk/virtual/virtio_fs/virtio_fs.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/disk/virtual/virtio_fs/virtio_fs.cpp
index b866173cab..3081719270 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/disk/virtual/virtio_fs/virtio_fs.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/disk/virtual/virtio_fs/virtio_fs.cpp
@@ -48,8 +48,11 @@
 
 // Requests in flight. Each owns a slot: a page for the device-readable header
 // and arguments, a page for the device-writable header and reply, and one data
-// buffer, used in whichever direction the request moves its payload.
-#define SLOT_COUNT			8
+// buffer, used in whichever direction the request moves its payload. Eight
+// serialized a burst (a Tracker copy of a folder is create, data, attributes,
+// times for every file at once); thirty-two cost 4.25 MiB of the many the
+// machine has.
+#define SLOT_COUNT			32
 #define SLOT_IN_SIZE		B_PAGE_SIZE
 #define SLOT_OUT_SIZE		B_PAGE_SIZE
 #define SLOT_DATA_SIZE		(128 * 1024)
@@ -424,9 +427,12 @@ virtio_fs_init_driver(device_node* node, void** _cookie)
 		virtio_fs_teardown(info);
 		return status;
 	}
+	// one entry for the whole area proves it is one physical run before any
+	// request is ever built from the addresses below
 	physical_entry physical;
-	status = get_memory_map(address, B_PAGE_SIZE, &physical, 1);
+	status = get_memory_map(address, size, &physical, 1);
 	if (status != B_OK) {
+		ERROR("the slot area is not physically contiguous: %s\n", strerror(status));
 		virtio_fs_teardown(info);
 		return status;
 	}
